# GitHub Linguist overrides: the language bar should describe Servette — the
# Python program — and this repository now holds nothing else. The website moved
# to its own repository, so the rules that kept site/ and its end-to-end harness
# out of the bar named paths that no longer exist here.
#
# The bar reads Python because the program is Python: servette/__init__.py (the
# module, generated from the literate sources in src/), src/build.py, and
# tests/test.py. src/*.md is where that module is authored, but it is left as
# Markdown deliberately — counting it as Python too would count the same code
# twice, once as source and once as generated output.
#
# src/diagnostics.html is the authored form of the diagnostic page, inlined into
# the module by build.py. Excluded for the same reason src/*.md is not counted
# as Python: its content is already counted once, inside the generated module.
# Counting the source too would count the same bytes twice.
src/diagnostics.html linguist-documentation

# The module is generated, but it IS the program — reviewed, and shipped as the
# release artifact — so it must stay counted even if a Linguist heuristic ever
# starts reading its generated-file banner.
servette/__init__.py -linguist-generated
